Suggests: gddrescue
Description: Archive, Record, Verify: long-term personal archiving on discs
 arv keeps a personal archive's record over decades: collections with their
 history, what is archived on which disc, every copy's place, and when it was
 last checked. It makes self-describing Blu-ray disc images: plain files, a
 BagIt bag, the catalogue of the whole archive, the source of the tools that
 made it, and dvdisaster-compatible RS03 error correction, readable without arv.
 .
 Experimental: the disc format is a draft (0.5). Keep your data where it is
 and treat discs made with this as an extra copy while you test it.
 .
 Recommends python3 for the browser interface (arv gui), 7zip for reading
 images in checks, git for the tool source on each disc, and xorriso for
 burning; gddrescue reads damaged discs into images.
